              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 4,
                "start": 4
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Respondent Aimee Stephens, according to Mr. Cole, Aimee Stephens, a transgender woman, was fired after announcing her gender identity, which constitutes sex discrimination."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Cole",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "cf1a12f36de8976e980e1ca7c913d4bc71463d6a7a404e2c6a252a883a4a191e",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-cf1a12f36de8-0001-0000"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 24,
                "start": 24
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Cole, the Sixth Circuit said the reasons for firing extended beyond the dress code, and Harris Homes conceded that she would have been fired even if she complied with the dress code."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Cole",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "cf1a12f36de8976e980e1ca7c913d4bc71463d6a7a404e2c6a252a883a4a191e",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-cf1a12f36de8-0001-0003"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 25,
                "start": 25
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Cole, recognizing transgender people\u2019s right to exist in the workplace does not end dress codes or restrooms."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "General Francisco",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "cf1a12f36de8976e980e1ca7c913d4bc71463d6a7a404e2c6a252a883a4a191e",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-cf1a12f36de8-0002-0000"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 46,
                "start": 46
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to General Francisco, gender identity is a broad concept."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "General Francisco",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "cf1a12f36de8976e980e1ca7c913d4bc71463d6a7a404e2c6a252a883a4a191e",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-cf1a12f36de8-0002-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 47,
                "start": 47
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to General Francisco, sex and gender identity are different traits, and Congress lists them separately in anti\u2011discrimination statutes."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "General Francisco",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "cf1a12f36de8976e980e1ca7c913d4bc71463d6a7a404e2c6a252a883a4a191e",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-cf1a12f36de8-0002-0002"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 48,
                "start": 48
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to General Francisco, the difference between a transgender man and a cisgender man is that one identifies with his biological sex and the other with the opposite, a meaningful distinction not based on stereotypes."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "General Francisco",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "cf1a12f36de8976e980e1ca7c913d4bc71463d6a7a404e2c6a252a883a4a191e",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-cf1a12f36de8-0002-0003"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 50,
                "start": 50
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to General Francisco, transgender men and cisgender men are not similarly situated because they do not share the same trait."
        }
